  "summary": "Toledo City Council voted 8-4 to approve a one-year extension of the city's contract with Flock Group Inc. for the Toledo Police Department's use of license plate cameras. Supporters called the cameras a valuable police tool, while four dissenting council members cited privacy concerns and resident opposition.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "After weeks of debate over public safety and privacy concerns, Toledo City Council approved a one-year extension of the city's contract with Flock Group Inc. on Tuesday.",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    },
    {
      "quote": "I am not in the mindset to take tools away from police that actually help our community",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "I support TPD in all that they do, but we do need to listen to the residents and look at what is happening across our country",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    }
